// Every operation the frontend needs, as one named command taking a JSON object of arguments and
// answering JSON -- the Ziman side of what the Tauri shell's `src-tauri/src/commands.rs` did
// before it was deleted on 2026-11-11.
//
// **Command-shaped, not REST, and that is the point.** The frontend calls these through Tauri's
// `invoke(name, args)` today, where `args` is an object of named arguments and the answer is the
// serde JSON of a return value. Keeping that exact shape means the frontend's whole move from a
// desktop shell to this server is `invoke` becoming one `fetch` in `api.ts` -- one function, not 26
// new URLs to design, argue about and then get wrong. A REST surface would be a second API to keep
// in step with the first for no gain: nothing but curly's own frontend will ever call this, it is
// not a public contract, and the resource-shaped version of `resolve_default_project` is a fiction.
//
// **An argument name here is the JavaScript spelling, so `envName` and not `env_name`.** Tauri
// converts a camelCase key from JS to its snake_case Rust parameter; there is no such layer here,
// so the wire name is what `api.ts` already writes. Renaming them to snake_case would be a second
// change to the frontend on top of the transport, in the one file this port must not churn.
//
// **`save_bytes` is deliberately absent.** It writes bytes to a path the user picked in a native
// save dialog -- an affordance of a desktop shell, not of a server, and a server that wrote to an
// arbitrary path on the host because a web page asked it to would be a straightforward hole. In a
// browser that operation is a download, which is the frontend's job (a Blob and an `<a download>`),
// so there is nothing for this module to expose. `docs/GUI.md` records it as the one bridge command
// with no server equivalent.
//
// Each command is a plain function from arguments to an answer, so the whole surface is testable
// against a temporary storage root without binding a socket -- `server/serve` is the only part that
// needs one. Shapes `core/` does not already encode live in `server/wire`.
